<title>USA: CSCE to raise margins on all cocoa contracts.</title>
<headline>CSCE to raise margins on all cocoa contracts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange Inc said Tuesday that effective March 12 it will raise margins on all cocoa contracts to $700, an increase of $300 from current levels.</p>
<p>For customers who are not exchange members or a member of the trade, margins will be 140 percent above trade rates, CSCE said.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Avidan, New York Commodities Desk, 212 859 1640))</p>
